The vulnerability is clearly present in this commit. In the `reg_ch_c_cntxt_1_fmask` array (lines 28-31), the field identifier used is `[ERINDEX]` instead of the version-specific `[CH_ERINDEX]`. The array shows:


static const u32 reg_ch_c_cntxt_1_fmask[] = {
	[CH_R_LENGTH]					= GENMASK(23, 0),
	[ERINDEX]					= GENMASK(31, 24),
};


According to the vulnerability root cause, this should use `[CH_ERINDEX]` instead of `[ERINDEX]` for IPA v5.0+. The incorrect field identifier causes the event ring index field to not be properly programmed. This is a bug-introducing commit because it introduces the vulnerable construct (wrong field identifier) without the fix.
